# Company Outreach Email — Hard Requirement

This template exists to pitch websites to real companies that already have trust (Google reviews, search traffic, local reputation) but lack a strong site.

After the demo site ships **and** `quality-gate/report.md` says **SHIP**, open a GitHub issue that drafts a polite outreach email. Do not send the email yourself.

## Issue

- Create with `gh issue create`
- Title: `Outreach draft: <Company Name> pitch email`
- Body order (required):
  1. **Company email** (`To:`) — real address from the brief / research. If none found: `Company email: not found — needs manual lookup`. Never invent one.
  2. Short findings bullets (include quality-gate SHIP + demo URL)
  3. Copy/paste draft email in a `text` fence
- Also open/update `Demo takedown: <Company> by <takedownAt>`
- If `gh` fails: write `outreach-email-draft.md` with the same order, commit it, and note the failure

## Email must cover (keep it short)

1. Specific praise from real findings (reviews, reputation). Quote one real review only if the brief has it.
2. Why a website helps a trusted business convert attention into clear contact and choice.
3. Complimentary unsolicited demo URL for the built site.
4. Offer to improve once they share missing assets (logo, photos, services, contact details, colours).
5. Plain-language SEO: helping them show up when people search for what they offer nearby.
6. Pricing exact: **R150 per month** or **R4 000 once-off**, free maintenance for **2 years**, domain **excluded**.
7. Takedown: remove anytime on request; auto-remove in **2 weeks** to avoid customer confusion.
8. Close with `tech@jmrsquared.com` and `https://tech.jmrsquared.com/`

## Writing rules

- Human, polite, warm. Make them proud of their business.
- No AI tells ("I hope this finds you well", leverage/unlock/seamless, em dashes, hype stacks).
- No invented review counts, quotes, facts, or email addresses.
- Half a page max. One clear ask: reply if they want to keep or refine the demo.
